# These tests fail because BraveThemeService::GetIsGrayscale() intentionally
# returns true whenever ThemeService::GetIsBaseline() is true (we replace the
# baseline palette with grayscale), so key.user_color_source resolves to
# kGrayscale instead of the kBaseline the tests expect for the non-system,
# non-device-theme cases, DevTools' userColorSource is "baseline-grayscale"
# instead of "baseline-default", and the theme source tests' assertion that the
# baseline theme isn't grayscale fails.
